      "message": "Wouldn\u0027t this be better off done by the caller?\n\nIf `pkvm_remap_range()` is supposed to preserve the buffer contents across different memory attributes, then we\u0027d also need to do maintenance when converting from non-cacheable to cacheable (to invalidate stale clean lines). However, I don\u0027t think the IOMMU reclaim path requires that, so I reckon it\u0027s probably best to defer the CMOs to the caller, who knows whether or not the buffer contents needs to be preserved.\n\nWDYT?",
